From b5ff55b716a04bfdcf86553a283697b65578ce8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CNY Healthcare <cnyhealthymall@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:44:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(send): require confirm for every uncountable fan-out,
 not just broadcast
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`estimateRecipients()` returned 0 for narrowcast and broadcast — the two
transports LINE gives no pre-send recipient count for. That 0 flowed into
`checkQuota()`, where it can neither exceed `remaining` nor cross the 95%
threshold, so the Quota Guardian returned ok unconditionally. The only real
gate left was `"everyone" in params.target`, which covers `{ everyone: true }`
and nothing else.

Net effect: `target: { filter: {...} }` and `target: { audience: "..." }`
reached the whole matching audience with no confirmation and no quota check —
in one tool call, from a model interpreting a sentence like "ส่งโปรให้ลูกค้า
ผู้หญิงกรุงเทพ". The file's own comment already says a broadcast cannot be
unsent; the same is true of a narrowcast.

Fixed at the root rather than by extending the target-key list:

- `estimateRecipients()` now returns `number | "unknown"`.
- `checkQuota()` accepts `ProjectedMessages = number | "unknown"` and treats
  "unknown" as always requiring confirm — evaluated BEFORE the unlimited-plan
  shortcut, because the gate exists for irreversibility, not for quota.
- `line_send_message` refuses an unconfirmed "unknown" send before the quota
  round-trip, so a refused send costs zero further LINE API calls. The gate
  reads the transport, not a hand-listed set of target keys, so a target shape
  added later inherits it. `checkQuota` still enforces the rule as a backstop.
- Outputs stop inventing a count: `recipient_count_estimated` /
  `projected_recipients` are omitted for these transports and a new
  `recipients_unknown: true` flag is set. v2.2.2 reported 0 recipients on a
  successful broadcast.
- dry_run surfaces the confirm requirement up front, where it costs nothing.

Tests: 22 added across the e2e suite and the Quota Guardian guardrails —
both narrowcast shapes refused unconfirmed with zero /narrowcast and zero
/quota traffic, both sending under confirm, the unlimited-plan path, dry_run
and draft behaviour, and multicast proven unaffected.
